$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=holfacx  LOC_AFTER=?

* The local factorisation of a holomorphic function at a point where not all Taylor coefficients vanish: for the least index n with a nonzero coefficient, F is ( z - P ) ^ n times a function holomorphic on D and nonzero at P.  Re-proof of ~ holfac keeping the Taylor characterisation of n and without a distinct-variable condition between C and j or y.

